# bundle-contract.json is a TWO-REPO FILE PINNED BY ITS BYTES. The same document
# lives here and at research-app/web/src/lib/bundle-contract.json, and
# tests/test_log_noise_0819.py sha256s it with read_bytes() against a constant
# so that a one-sided edit goes red in each repo's OWN suite, with no second
# checkout involved. That only works if every checkout holds the same bytes.
#
# This box is core.autocrlf=true and this repo had no .gitattributes, so the
# file came out of git with CRLF and hashed to a13f96c1... against the pinned
# f6b3276e... — a deterministic Windows-only failure whose message reads
# "bundle-contract.json changed. Update BOTH repos' copies and BOTH digests",
# which if followed would push a CRLF-derived digest that then fails everywhere
# else. Pin LF so the bytes are the same everywhere and the digest means what it
# says.
bundle-contract.json text eol=lf
